# Component Patterns

## Editorial design language

Bright.Experience uses a single editorial design language. Every authenticated page composes from the same chassis — never roll a bespoke layout.

### Page chassis primitives (in `src/components/brand/`)

- `EditionShell` — theme wrapper. All authenticated pages start here.
- `EditionChrome` — sticky top bar with breadcrumbs + right slot (notifications, user menu).
- `RidgeHero` — hero with seeded `RidgeArtwork`, eyebrow, title, subtitle, optional `rightSlot`.
- `EditionBody` — main content wrapper with the standard horizontal rhythm.
- `EditionFooter` — bottom bar with brand lockup and Cmd+K hint.
- `EventPageShell` — convenience wrapper for `/events/[id]/*` sub-pages. Pass `event`, `section`, `title`, `subtitle`.
- `AdminPageShell` — same shape for internal `/admin/*` and adjacent pages.

For any new event sub-page, use `EventPageShell`. For any new internal admin view, use `AdminPageShell`. Never compose `EditionShell` + `EditionChrome` + `RidgeHero` by hand unless the page is genuinely one-of-one.

### Editorial primitives (in `src/components/brand/editorial.tsx`)

- `EditorialEyebrow` — tracked uppercase DM Sans Medium label. Use this anywhere we'd have used a small heading or a section eyebrow. Pass `accent` for the cobalt brand colour.
- `Hairline` — 1px gradient rule that separates editorial sections without the weight of a card border. Pass `orientation="vertical"` for column dividers.

### Generative artwork

- `RidgeArtwork` — deterministic SVG, seeded by an event id or route key. Use this in place of decorative blur orbs. Pass `lines` and `amplitude` to dial visual weight.
- `EditionPlate` — compact card representing a single event. Used in event lists, the "Your other events" rail, partner dashboards. Has its own scoped ridge.

## shadcn/ui Usage

- Always use shadcn primitives for standard UI elements (`Button`, `Input`, `Label`, `Textarea`, `Dialog`, `Select`, `Table`, `Badge`, `Card`).
- Import from `@/components/ui/` — never install UI libraries that duplicate shadcn functionality.
- Use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for all conditional classNames.
- Extend shadcn components via composition, not modification of the `ui/` files.

### Variant cheat sheet

| Need | Use |
|------|-----|
| Primary CTA | `<Button variant="brand">` (or `default` — same gradient) |
| Secondary CTA | `<Button variant="glass">` |
| Tertiary CTA | `<Button variant="ghost">` |
| Destructive action | `<Button variant="destructive">` |
| Hoverable card | `<Card interactive>` |
| Hero card | `<Card tone="glass">` — max one per page |
| Body card | `<Card>` (default `tone="glass"`) or `<Card tone="subtle">` |
| Success badge | `<Badge variant="success">` |
| Warning badge | `<Badge variant="warning">` |
| Destructive badge | `<Badge variant="destructive">` |
| Info badge | `<Badge variant="info">` |
| Muted/neutral badge | `<Badge variant="muted">` |

### Banned patterns

- **No legacy `.btn`/`.card`/`.badge`/`.input` CSS classes.** They were removed in May 2026. Use the shadcn primitives instead.
- **No ad-hoc `rounded-2xl` / `rounded-3xl`.** Use `var(--radius-card)`, `var(--radius-control)`, or `var(--radius-chip)`.
- **No `bg-clip-text`** outside of the brand mark itself.
- **No more than one `tone="glass"` `<Card>` per page.**
- **No emoji** in product UI unless explicitly added by the user.
- **No "book/chapter/edition" metaphor.** That language was removed in May 2026 — use "events", "stages", "milestones".

## Component Structure

```tsx
/** Brief description of what this component does */
"use client"; // only if needed

import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

interface MyComponentProps { /* typed props */ }

export function MyComponent({ ...props }: MyComponentProps) {
  return ( /* JSX */ );
}
```

## Rules

- Prefer Server Components. Only add `"use client"` when the component needs interactivity.
- Never pass functions or React components across the server/client boundary.
- Keep components focused: if it renders more than one distinct section, split it.
- Co-locate types with components when they are only used by that component.
- Files cap at ~200 lines. Split if longer.
